  Stage_24528_Desc = {
    Text = "No matter what befalls, no matter how much is transformed—your call will always be heard."
  },
  Stage_24528_Name = {
    Text = "Not Goodbye"
  },
  Stage_24529_Desc = {
    Text = "Once, twice, thrice—Sisyphus pushes his boulder, ascending in vain toward a summit that cannot be reached."
  },
  Stage_24529_Name = {Text = "Sisyphus"},
  Stage_24530_Desc = {
    Text = "The once-familiar girl has become a stranger. This cold, distant figure—can she truly be the Ramona you knew?"
  },
  Stage_24530_Name = {Text = "All In"},
  Stage_24531_Desc = {
    Text = "An ordinary day begins with an extraordinary dream."
  },
  Stage_24531_Name = {
    Text = "Rainlike Tears"
  },
  Stage_24532_Desc = {
    Text = "The once-familiar girl has become a stranger. This cold, distant figure—can she truly be the Ramona you knew?"
  },
  Stage_24532_Name = {Text = "All In"},
  Stage_24533_Desc = {
    Text = "The once-familiar girl has become a stranger. This cold, distant figure—can she truly be the Ramona you knew?"
  },
  Stage_24533_Name = {Text = "All In"},
  Stage_34716_Desc = {
    Text = "A sudden twist, an unexpected turn, a shift in the story—the Keeper cannot help but feel that this, at times, describes themselves."
  },
  Stage_34716_Name = {
    Text = "III: Plot Rotation"
  },
  Stage_34717_Desc = {
    Text = "This is a word even Ramona hadn't heard. With the aid of some elderly Awakeners, everyone finally came to understand: sometimes, a good cry is the only remedy for a troubled spirit."
  },
  Stage_34717_Name = {
    Text = "II: Catharsis"
  },
  Stage_34718_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The theoretical book Casiah found states: the time of the story cannot exceed one day, and the stage cannot exceed one location...
The Keeper gave up reading this. After all, sometimes even one day is not enough for completing a post-class assignment paper on "Dissolution and Cataclysm Prevention".]]
  },
  Stage_34718_Name = {
    Text = "I: Classical Unities"
  },
  Stage_34719_Desc = {
    Text = [[
The theoretical volume found by Casiah reads: the pyramid model concerns itself with the resolution of a crisis.
Yet not every crisis finds resolution in reality. They are concealed beneath the illusion of peace, festering in the dark, until they erupt into a new "pyramid."]]
  },
  Stage_34719_Name = {
    Text = "VII: Drama's Apex"
  },
  Stage_34720_Desc = {
    Text = "At a story's end, a character must show growth or transformation. Yet in life, the arc has a way of bending back into a circle."
  },
  Stage_34720_Name = {
    Text = "VI: Arc's Theorem"
  },
  Stage_34721_Desc = {
    Text = "A scene set in advance, a handful of familiar actors. The rest is up to inspiration and interaction."
  },
  Stage_34721_Name = {
    Text = "V: Masked Farce"
  },
  Stage_34722_Desc = {
    Text = "Do not bombard the audience's mind at every moment; leave them space to think—ideally, leave them in complete stillness. If only Doll could apply this during class, the Keeper murmured, and everyone agreed."
  },
  Stage_34722_Name = {
    Text = "IV: Quiet Instant"
  },
