    Text = "Cité is a city of flowers and poetry, where a good poem may be exchanged for a bouquet.\nThat was her first poem. That was the first rose she grew.\nWhen their hands met, the girl's radiant face outshone every flower and every verse."
  },
  Stage_55164_Name = {
    Text = "First Bloom: Part V"
  },
  Stage_55165_Desc = {
    Text = "Cité is a city of flowers and poetry, where a good poem may be exchanged for a bouquet.\nThat was her first poem. That was the first rose she grew.\nWhen their hands met, the girl's radiant face outshone every flower and every verse."
  },
  Stage_55165_Name = {
    Text = "First Bloom: Part II"
  },
  Stage_55166_Desc = {
    Text = "The celebrated poem brought everything; she blushed at her friend's praise. Her verse had finally spared her friend from suffering—or so she believed.\nWhat she did not hear was that the seeds of malice had already been sown, lying in wait to entwine the roses and destroy them."
  },
  Stage_55166_Name = {
    Text = "Verses Aflame: Madness"
  },
  Stage_55166_StageInitStateText = {Text = "Finale"},
  Stage_55167_Desc = {
    Text = "Cité is a city of flowers and poetry, where a good poem may be exchanged for a bouquet.\nThat was her first poem. That was the first rose she grew.\nWhen their hands met, the girl's radiant face outshone every flower and every verse."
  },
  Stage_55167_Name = {
    Text = "First Bloom: Part I"
  },
  Stage_55391_Desc = {
    Text = "\"Let me trade you the first rose for your first poem.\""
  },
  Stage_55391_Name = {Text = "Psalm 1843"},
  Stage_55392_Desc = {
    Text = "The Garden is a puzzle, and Spring its last piece."
  },
  Stage_55392_Name = {
    Text = "Lingering Scent"
  },
  Stage_55393_Desc = {
    Text = "\"Let me trade you the first rose for your first poem.\""
  },
  Stage_55393_Name = {Text = "Psalm 1843"},
  Stage_55394_Desc = {
    Text = [[
No mourning. No wind.
Only the poet's residual ink, and the death knell tolling for the garden.]]
  },
  Stage_55394_Name = {
    Text = "Garden Dirge"
  },
  Stage_55395_Desc = {
    Text = "The statue is the king's rhetoric; silence is the statue's."
  },
  Stage_55395_Name = {
    Text = "Statuary Rhetoric"
  },
  Stage_55396_Desc = {
    Text = "They gaze at each other across the garden.\nWithin it lie countless paths—every one that is hers, a divergence from every one that is the other's."
  },
  Stage_55396_Name = {
    Text = "Garden of Forked Paths"
  },
  Stage_55397_Desc = {
    Text = "Bid farewell to bones in the first funeral, and to time in the second."
  },
  Stage_55397_Name = {
    Text = "Belated Funeral"
  },
  Stage_55398_Desc = {
    Text = [[
Excellent poetry immerses the reader in its world.
Or so classical aesthetic theory would have it.]]
  },
  Stage_55398_Name = {Text = "The Poet"},
  Stage_55399_Desc = {
    Text = "The blossoms of Cité extend their invitation, beckoning you to join them in this dream."
  },
  Stage_55399_Name = {
    Text = "City of Blossoms"
  },
  Stage_55400_Desc = {
    Text = "What people call home is nothing more than a long-standing lie."
  },
  Stage_55400_Name = {Text = "Home"},
  Stage_55401_Desc = {
    Text = "\"Let me trade you the first rose for your first poem.\""
  },
  Stage_55401_Name = {Text = "Psalm 1843"},
  Stage_55551_Desc = {
    Text = "This snow mountain is alive; howls reverberate through its passes—it is calling for its daughter.\nCome, come quickly.\nIs it the daughter who goes to the mother, or the mother who goes to the daughter?\nAt the summit, two hollow, empty stomachs finally meet."
  },
  Stage_55551_Name = {
